   "text": "This structure is ibogaine, the 10-methoxy ibogamine skeleton, and I read the stereochemistry from the four wedge/hash bonds in the drawing.\n\n**Skeleton**\n- A 5-methoxyindole unit sits on the right: a benzene ring carrying OMe, fused to a pyrrole ring with an NH.\n- The indole C3 carries a CH2CH2 chain that leads to the tertiary amine N.\n- The indole C2 is bonded to a CH, which I call C_d. This carbon carries a hashed H.\n- C_d also bonds to a CH2 and to the CH next to N, which I call C_b. C_b has a hashed H.\n- The CH2 leads to C_c, a bridgehead CH with a wedged H. C_c is bonded to a CH2 that runs to C_a and to another CH2 that goes to N, giving the isoquinuclidine cage.\n- C_a is a CH with a hashed H and an ethyl group. It is bonded to C_b.\n\n**Stereocentres**\nI assigned each of the four centres from the drawn wedge/hash direction and the neighbour order in the SMILES. Working through them gave C_a as @, C_c as @@, C_d as @@ and C_b as @. I did not cross-check these against a known ibogaine SMILES.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@H]1C[C@@H]2C[C@@H]3[C@H]1N(C2)CCc1c3[nH]c2ccc(OC)cc12"
